    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="0912" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.796/200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Legation in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-29T10:00:00+08:00">April 29, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—5:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. I am reliably informed that within past 3 days a meeting of representatives
                    of the Foreign Office, the Ministry of Communications <pb facs="0913" n="801"
                        xml:id="pg801"/> and the Military Affairs Commission called to discuss
                    questions of possible cooperation by China in development of overseas
                    transportation, decided Chinese Government would not for the present grant
                    landing rights to any foreign aviation concerns because of fear that concessions
                    to western airline companies would make it impossible to refuse similar requests
                    from Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
